2:T6bb,{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"How do I find trusted independent kitchen fitters in St Albans?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Compare written, itemised quotes, check the full scope of work and ask who will handle plumbing, electrical work, tiling and cabinet installation. A site visit can help confirm measurements and the work required before booking."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How much do independent kitchen fitters charge in St Albans?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Costs vary widely. As a rough guide, fitting and associated renovation work may cost several thousand pounds, with larger projects typically costing around £5,000 to £15,000 or more, excluding some units and appliances. Every project differs, so get a free, no-obligation quote for accurate pricing."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Do kitchen fitters also connect appliances?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Some do, but the scope varies. Ask specifically whether appliance connections, plumbing alterations and electrical work are included and who will carry out the work."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Should I buy the kitchen before booking a fitter?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Not necessarily. It can be sensible to involve the fitter before ordering, so measurements, service positions, delivery details and installation requirements can be checked first."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How long does a kitchen renovation take?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The programme depends on the size of the kitchen, product availability, layout changes and preparation work. Ask for a project-specific estimate."}}]}7:["slug","independent-kitchen-fitters-st-albans","d"]
